{{Quote|When in trouble, Gungans go to sacred place.|Jar Jar Binks|<ref name="Star Wars Episode I: The Phantom Menace" />}}
The '''Gungan Sacred Place''',<ref name="BMF 41">{{BuildFalconCite|41|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref> also known simply as the '''Sacred Place''',<ref name="On the Front Lines">''[[Star Wars: On the Front Lines]]''</ref> was in an ancient [[forest]].<ref name="Forces of Nature">{{InsiderCite|216|Forces of Nature: The Wild Spaces and Wilder Creatures of the Star Wars Galaxy|Forces of Nature: The Wild Spaces and Wilder Creatures of the ''Star Wars'' Galaxy}}</ref> It became sacred to the [[Gungan]]s, a sanctuary for troubled times. During the [[Trade Federation]]'s [[invasion of Naboo]], [[Queen]] [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]] was guided there by [[Jar Jar Binks]] to meet [[Boss]] [[Rugor Nass|Nass]], and together they [[Boss Meetup|formulated]] a [[Battle of Naboo|plan]] to retake their [[homeworld]].<ref name="Star Wars Episode I: The Phantom Menace" /> After the [[Battle of Naboo]], the Gungans took their fallen [[Militiagung|warriors]] to the sacred place. They invited Amidala to attend the [[funeral]], though as there was no [[time]] the queen sent [[Eirtaé]] and [[Yané]] in her place.<ref name="Queen's Peril">''[[Queen's Peril]]''</ref>

{{Loc-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
According to [[Forces of Nature: The Wild Spaces and Wilder Creatures of the Star Wars Galaxy|Forces of Nature: The Wild Spaces and Wilder Creatures of the ''Star Wars'' Galaxy]], the Gungans and Naboo humans coming together in an ancient forest is an example of the "symbiotic relationship" of nature and all the life forms who live within it. This symbiotic concept was developed by [[George Lucas]] for the [[Prequel trilogy]].<ref name="Forces of Nature" />

